<title>CANADA: Second Cup Ltd June 29 Q4 turns to loss. [CORRECTED 15:40 GMT]</title>
<headline>Second Cup Ltd June 29 Q4 turns to loss. [CORRECTED 15:40 GMT]</headline>
<dateline>TORONTO 1996-09-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Three months ended June 29.</p>
<p>				1996			    1995</p>
<p> Shr	   loss	C$0.54   profit	C$0.09</p>
<p> Net	   loss	 6,271   profit	   575</p>
<p> Revs			70,836		   24,929</p>
<p>			  12  MONTHS (corrects from &quot;six months&quot;)</p>
<p> Shr	   loss	C$0.25   profit	C$0.37</p>
<p> Net	   loss	 2,366   profit	 2,249</p>
<p> Revs		     214,358		   80,675</p>
<p> Avg shrs		   9,451		    6,108</p>
<p>(All data above 000s except per share numbers)</p>
<p>Note: Results in 1996 include 53 weeks ended June 29, while 1995 results are for 52 weeks ended June 24.</p>
<p>Year end results for 1996 include a C$4.9 million provision for planned closure of the firm's seven Coffee Plantation stores in Texas and California. It also includes transitional expenses related to financing activities for newly acquired Gloria Jean's Gourmet Coffees and Second Cup.</p>
<p>-- Reuters Toronto Bureau (416) 941-8100</p>
